======================================================================
PART J -- FAILURE HANDLING AND RECOVERY
======================================================================
SCENARIO 1: ERP down after Fineract success
----------------------------------------------------------------------
BEFORE: loan=Approved  ERP-entry-exists=404
DURING: disbursing with ERP down...
{"status":"NEEDS_RECONCILIATION","external_reference":"REF-S1-DISB-1791470706"} -> HTTP 202
  -> Fineract succeeded (money moved), ERP leg failed: status is NEEDS_RECONCILIATION, not a plain FAILED --
     a resend of the SAME reference replays NEEDS_RECONCILIATION (never re-disburses):
{"status":"NEEDS_RECONCILIATION","external_reference":"REF-S1-DISB-1791470706"} -> HTTP 202
AFTER (still stuck): loan=Active  ERP-entry-exists=404
RECOVERING: calling the admin recovery sweep (retries only the ERP leg, never re-calls Fineract)...
{"processed":1,"results":[{"external_reference":"REF-S1-DISB-1791470706","status_before":"NEEDS_RECONCILIATION","status_after":"COMPLETED","result_status_code":201}]}
AFTER RECOVERY: loan=Active  ERP-entry-exists=200
======================================================================
SCENARIO 2: Fineract down
----------------------------------------------------------------------
BEFORE: loan=Approved
DURING: disbursing with Fineract down...
{"error_code":"UPSTREAM_ERROR","message":"Fineract unreachable: simulated: fineract_disburse down (fault injection)","correlation_id":"de1202ca-ff4a-4eb8-a513-6c848d15c51f"} -> HTTP 502
  -> clean 502 UPSTREAM_ERROR, nothing persisted at Fineract:
AFTER: loan=Approved (unchanged -- confirms nothing was persisted)
Safe to retry? Yes -- a fresh reference for the same loan now (Fineract 'back up') succeeds normally:
{"loan_reference":"LN-S2-1791470713","status":"Active","fineract_transaction_id":54} -> HTTP 201
AFTER RETRY: loan=Active
======================================================================
SCENARIO 3: Fineract timeout after sending (the request DID land at Fineract; we just never saw the response)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
BEFORE: loan=Approved
DURING: disbursing (real call lands at Fineract; our client simulates a timeout instead of seeing the response)...
{"loan_reference":"LN-S3-1791470718","status":"Active","fineract_transaction_id":56} -> HTTP 201
  -> Not a blind retry: we looked Fineract up by externalId (=REF-S3-DISB-1791470718), found the real disbursement,
     and completed the whole flow (including the ERP leg) within this same request.
AFTER: loan=Active  ERP-entry-exists=200
======================================================================
SCENARIO 4: ERP timeout after the entry was written
----------------------------------------------------------------------
DURING: disbursing (ERP really writes the entry; our client simulates a timeout instead of seeing the response)...
{"status":"NEEDS_RECONCILIATION","external_reference":"REF-S4-DISB-1791470722"} -> HTTP 202
  -> reports NEEDS_RECONCILIATION even though the entry already exists (we don't yet know that ourselves):
RECOVERING: admin recovery sweep retries the ERP leg -- hits Mock ERP's OWN idempotency, no duplicate:
{"processed":1,"results":[{"external_reference":"REF-S4-DISB-1791470722","status_before":"NEEDS_RECONCILIATION","status_after":"COMPLETED","result_status_code":201}]}
PROOF: exactly one journal entry exists for REF-S4-DISB-1791470722:
1 entry/entries
======================================================================
SCENARIO 5: crash between Fineract success and the ERP call -- recovered on restart
----------------------------------------------------------------------
DURING: disbursing (simulates the process dying right after the Fineract leg, before the ERP leg)...
{"status":"NEEDS_RECONCILIATION","external_reference":"REF-S5-DISB-1791470726"} -> HTTP 202
BEFORE RESTART: loan=Active  ERP-entry-exists=404 (stuck)
Restarting the container (simulates recovery after a real crash, not a manual recovery call)...
AFTER RESTART (no manual action taken): loan=Active  ERP-entry-exists=200
  -> the startup sweep found the stuck row and completed it automatically before the app even finished starting.
======================================================================
